{"id": "EUVD-2014-9825", "enisaUuid": "76b5e26e-6075-33d0-b414-05cbcc988c80", "description": "Blogroll Fun plugin for WordPress before 0.8.5 contains a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to inject scripts through the 'k' parameter in blogroll.php. Attackers can craft GET requests to /wp-content/plugins/blogroll-fun/blogroll.php with malicious 'k' values that are echoed unsanitized, executing JavaScript in victims' browsers. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-19.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T20:31:22", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://codevigilant.com/disclosure/wp-plugin-blogroll-fun-a3-cross-site-scripting-xss/", "https://www.acunetix.com/vulnerabilities/web/wordpress-plugin-blogroll-fun-show-last-post-and-last-update-time-cross-site-scripting-0-8-4/", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/wp-blogroll-fun-xss.yaml", "https://wordpress.org/plugins/blogroll-fun/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/blogroll-fun-wordpress-plugin-0.8.5-reflected-xss-via-blogroll-php"], "aliases": ["CVE-2014-125132", "GHSA-vcg9-96r7-4fvx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "991282a7-90d2-334e-badd-2e45979df6cf", "product": {"name": "Blogroll Fun", "vendor": {"name": "Jason Newman"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.8.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "faa26814-1e47-3e94-97c5-b3cf474fffca", "vendor": {"name": "Jason Newman"}}], "isExploited": false}